# shadcn/ui + Tailwind

Build every user-facing UI with **shadcn/ui** primitives and **Tailwind CSS** utilities.
Do not invent custom buttons, inputs, dialogs, menus, tables, or other controls when a
shadcn component exists.

This project uses shadcn/ui on **Base UI** (not Radix), `base-nova` style, Lucide icons.
Config is in `components.json`. Tokens live in `src/app/globals.css`.

## Use the catalog, not raw HTML

Prefer `@/components/ui/*` over native elements. Typical mappings:

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Actions, links styled as actions | `Button` / `buttonVariants` |
| Text fields | `Input` + `Field`, `FieldLabel`, `FieldError` |
| Surfaces | `Card`, `CardHeader`, `CardTitle`, `CardDescription`, `CardContent` |
| Modals | `Dialog` |
| Status | `Badge` |
| Data grids | `Table` |
| Dividers | `Separator` |

If the needed primitive is missing (Select, Dropdown Menu, Tabs, Sheet, Tooltip,
Checkbox, Switch, Textarea, Pagination, Alert, Sonner, Sidebar, Breadcrumb, Avatar,
Command, Popover, Accordion, and the rest of the registry), **add it first**:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add @shadcn/select
```

Always use the `@shadcn/` namespace. A bare `add select` does nothing. If no files
appear, that name is not in the Base UI registry — pick the equivalent, do not
hand-roll a replacement.

Installed files live in `src/components/ui/`. Do not rewrite them unless the user
asks to change the design system.

## Component capabilities

Use the API the component already exposes. Do not reimplement variants with extra CSS.

- **Button**: `variant` (`default` `outline` `secondary` `ghost` `destructive` `link`) and
  `size` (`default` `xs` `sm` `lg` `icon` `icon-xs` `icon-sm` `icon-lg`). For a Next.js
  `Link` that should look like a button, apply `buttonVariants()`.
- **Icons**: Lucide (`lucide-react`). Size through the component, not one-off CSS.
- **Forms**: there is no `Form` primitive on Base UI. Compose `FieldSet`, `FieldGroup`,
  `Field`, `FieldLabel`, `FieldDescription`, `FieldError`. Server Actions + Zod.
  `FieldError` takes `{ message }[]`. Do not add `react-hook-form` unless asked.

```tsx
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { buttonVariants } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

// ❌ BAD — raw control, hardcoded color
<button className="bg-[#171717] px-3 py-2 text-white">Save</button>

// ✅ GOOD — shadcn + theme tokens
<Button variant="default" size="sm">Save</Button>
<Link href="/logout" className={cn(buttonVariants({ variant: "outline" }))}>
  Log out
</Link>
```

## Tailwind is the only styling layer

- Style layout, spacing, and typography with Tailwind utilities on `className`.
- No CSS modules, styled-components, or extra styling libraries.
- Merge classes with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`.
- Use semantic tokens (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`,
  `border-input`, `bg-primary`, `text-destructive`). Never hard-code hex colors.
- Tailwind v4 config belongs in `src/app/globals.css` only. Do not add `tailwind.config.*`.
